Changes to sing-box v1.14.4 (GNU GPL v3.0 or later), made by the unbraid authors, last on 2026-11-17:
a stand-in (fake) address is never handed to a second name while the range is unchanged: once the range is used
up, lookups of new names are answered with a server failure instead, an address that still names a domain is
skipped even when the saved position is older (a start moves past such addresses), an address whose name could not
be saved is not handed out (and the pool then counts as used up), a start whose saved position is missing or
unreadable keeps the names of its range instead of dropping them, a range whose names were lost with a damaged cache
file counts as used up (also for later starts, until a range change resets the cache), and libbox tells how many
addresses can still be handed out (FakeIPRemaining), so the app can move to a fresh range in time.
Applied by tools/build-libbox.sh; git apply skips these lines.

